    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391">

                <pb facs="0393" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.77/7–2444</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1039</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-24">July 24,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received August 7.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s telegram No. 409 of July 6, 1944 instructing the Legation to advise
                    the authorities concerned that the United States Government feels it unnecessary
                    to join in the proposed Irano-American-Soviet-British agreement on financial
                    responsibilities for the war-time operation of the Iranian State Railways. The
                    British Embassy was informed of this decision by letter dated July 12, a copy of
                    which was sent to the Soviet Embassy. To date, I have had no reply nor comment
                    from either Embassy.</p>
                <p>Since the Legation had never discussed the question with the Iranian authorities,
                    no notification of the Department’s decision has been made to the Ministry of
                    Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
